  "point": "On lopsided data with no balancing, the router just follows demand: the busiest single expert handles 17.6% of all traffic (4.2\u00d7 its fair share) and only 24 of 24 experts carry real load \u2014 the rest are nearly idle capacity you still paid to build and run. Add a small 'spread the load' incentive and the busiest drops to 12.1% (2.9\u00d7 fair share) with 24 of 24 active, trading a little routing precision (81%\u219274%) for even load. That trade is exactly why a real mixture-of-experts ships with a stability trick."
